00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.710
Hey Collider fans, I'm John Rocha.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.030
"The Meg" swims and chomps its way into

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.920
theaters this weekend and we thought

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.210
we'd count down the Top 5 Shark Movie Deaths.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.980
Now there have been many

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.890
memorable shark attacks on film

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.420
#Batman1966 #SharkRepellent

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.310
but we wanted to look at some

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.600
of the best deaths. A warning to all of

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.430
you: if you're squeamish then make sure

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.300
you've got a trash can nearby to drop

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.300
your Chum into

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.789
[Vomiting]

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.280
We start off our list with one of the

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.170
most horrific shark deaths on film, yet

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.760
one where we never even see a shark

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.890
Steven Spielberg's "Jaws" has scared

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.600
generations of film-goers for years.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.070
One of the many reasons why is the opening

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.540
scene of the movie: a young woman has

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.310
swum out into the ocean at night after

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.690
enjoying a beach campfire. The water is

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:57.400
peaceful and the buoy dings in the

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.620
distance. We got a peaceful easy feeling,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.060
but it doesn't last long - the young woman

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.890
is suddenly taken underwater three times

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.570
and begins to freak out, realizing the

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:06.100
terror she is in. The shark drags her

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.840
back and forth in the water. We hear

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.070
these horrible sounds of absolute terror

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.200
bursting out of her mouth.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.540
The attack lasts 45 seconds and

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.680
Spielberg (that crafty mofo) even teases

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.450
us that the young woman might escape

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.190
when she is dragged to the buoy and the

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.630
shark attack stops. The respit only

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.130
lasts a couple of seconds before the

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.229
shark returns and takes her underwater

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.340
to her death, the water is calm again and

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:25.330
we are left with a terror that will

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.160
carry us through the rest of the movie.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.080
Our #4 Movie Shark Death comes

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.060
from "Open Water" in the film a couple on

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.770
vacation Susan and Daniel gets stranded

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.150
when a tourist boat accident that leaves

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.430
them behind and they spend the movie

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.950
fighting off a shark in you guessed it

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:41.050
open water (boom, nailed it!) Susan's death

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.270
is a scary unsettling yet surprisingly

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:45.159
empowering one after daniel is attacked

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.540
earlier and eaten overnight Susan spots

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:48.190
Daniels remains floating in the water

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.810
the next morning she has almost no time

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.550
to grieve her loss however because she

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.560
also spies with her little eye something

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.970
that begins with an S and that's SHARKS.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.229
More have shown up to join Daniel's

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.640
attacker and are thrashing about

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:58.240
whipping themselves into a feeding

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.220
frenzy

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.350
realizing she is about to become a KFC

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.030
meal Susan makes the surprising decision

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.830
to take her air tanks and swimming

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:07.659
goggles off let them float away and

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.340
defiantly chooses to drown herself.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:10.899
Yeah there's no blood or ripping off

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.459
body parts but it's a powerful shark movie

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:14.019
death nonetheless. I mean what would you do?

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:15.459
#3 in our list is

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:17.320
